The provided class is a trivial implementation that immediately signals an error via `EmptyDisposable.error`. It contains no computational work, branching, or state changes that could vary in performance. Benchmarking such a no‑op/error‑propagation path would not yield useful performance insights, and any measured time would be dominated by JMH harness overhead rather than the code under test. Therefore, a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.